    "questionEn": "Each of the angles β and γ that a given line makes with the positive y - and z -axes, respectively, is half of the angle that this line makes with the positive x -axes. Then the sum of all possible values of the angle β is",
    "optionsEn": [
      "π 2",
      "π",
      "3 π 4",
      "3 π 2"
    ],
    "correctOptionIndex": 2,
    "explanationEn": "Let α be the angle the line makes with the positive x -axis. We are given β = γ = α 2 , so α = 2 β and γ = β . The direction cosines of a line satisfy cos 2 ⁡ α + cos 2 ⁡ β + cos 2 ⁡ γ = 1. Substituting the given relations, cos 2 ⁡ 2 β + 2 cos 2 ⁡ β = 1. Using 2 cos 2 ⁡ β = 1 + cos ⁡ 2 β , we get cos 2 ⁡ 2 β + cos ⁡ 2 β = 0 , cos ⁡ 2 β ( cos ⁡ 2 β + 1 ) = 0. Thus, cos ⁡ 2 β = 0 or cos ⁡ 2 β = − 1. Since direction angles lie in [ 0 , π ] and α = 2 β , we have 0 ≤ 2 β ≤ π . Hence the possible values are 2 β = π 2 or π , giving β = π 4 or π 2 . Their sum is π 4 + π 2 = 3 π 4 . So the correct choice is Option C .",
