    "questionEn": "Let A = { − 2 , − 1 , 0 , 1 , 2 , 3 } . Let R be a relation on A defined by x R y if and only if y = max { x , 1 } . Let l be the number of elements in R . Let m and n be the minimum number of elements required to be added in R to make it reflexive and symmetric relations, respectively. Then l + m + n is equal to",
