    "explanationEn": "Step 1: Balancing Forces on the Bob At equilibrium, the electric force ( q E ) pulling the bob toward the sheet is balanced by the weight of the bob ( m g ) pulling it down. Step 2: Formula for Electric Field Near Sheet The electric field ( E ) created by a large sheet of charge is given by E = σ 2 ε 0 . Step 3: Replace E in the Force Equation The equation from earlier becomes: q [ σ 2 ε 0 ] = m g Step 4: Solve for σ We solve for σ by rearranging: σ = 2 ε 0 m g q Step 5: Substitute the Values Put in the given values: ε 0 = 8.85 × 10 − 12 F/m, m = 100 mg = 100 × 10 − 6 kg, g = 10 m/s 2 , q = 10 × 10 − 6 C. So, σ = 2 × 8.85 × 10 − 12 × 100 × 10 − 6 × 10 10 × 10 − 6 Step 6: Calculate We do the multiplication and division: σ = 17.7 × 10 − 10 C / m 2 Step 7: Convert to nC/m 2 1 nC = 10 − 9 C , so σ = 1.77 nC / m 2",
