    "questionEn": "An air bubble of radius 0.1 cm lies at a depth of 20 cm below the free surface of a liquid of density 1000 kg / m 3 . If the pressure inside the bubble is 2100 N / m 2 greater than the atmospheric pressure, then the surface tension of the liquid in SI unit is (use g = 10 m / s 2 )",
