    "questionEn": "A solid sphere of mass ' m ' and radius ' r ' is allowed to roll without slipping from the highest point of an inclined plane of length ' L ' and makes an angle 30 ∘ with the horizontal. The speed of the particle at the bottom of the plane is v 1 . If the angle of inclination is increased to 45 ∘ while keeping L constant. Then the new speed of the sphere at the bottom of the plane is v 2 . The ratio v 2 1 : v 2 2 is",
