    "explanationEn": "α = lim x → ∞ [ ( e 1 − e ) ( 1 e − x 1 + x ) ] x . Begin by rewriting the expression inside the limit. Notice that x 1 + x = 1 − 1 1 + x , so 1 e − x 1 + x = 1 e − ( 1 − 1 1 + x ) = 1 e − 1 + 1 1 + x . Express the constant part as 1 − 1 e = e − 1 e , to obtain 1 e − x 1 + x = − e − 1 e + 1 1 + x . Multiplying by the prefactor, we have ( e 1 − e ) ( 1 e − x 1 + x ) = e 1 − e [ − e − 1 e + 1 1 + x ] . Split the expression: e 1 − e ⋅ ( − e − 1 e ) + e 1 − e ⋅ 1 1 + x = − e − 1 1 − e + e ( 1 − e ) ( 1 + x ) . Since 1 − e = − ( e − 1 ) , it follows that − e − 1 1 − e = − e − 1 − ( e − 1 ) = 1. Hence, the expression simplifies to 1 + e ( 1 − e ) ( 1 + x ) . Again, replacing 1 − e by − ( e − 1 ) , 1 + e − ( e − 1 ) ( 1 + x ) = 1 − e ( e − 1 ) ( 1 + x ) . Thus, the limit becomes α = lim x → ∞ ( 1 − e ( e − 1 ) ( 1 + x ) ) x . For large x , note that 1 + x ∼ x , so we approximate α = lim x → ∞ ( 1 − e ( e − 1 ) x ) x . Recall the limit lim x → ∞ ( 1 − a x ) x = e − a , with a = e e − 1 . Therefore, α = e − e e − 1 . Taking the natural logarithm, ln ⁡ α = − e e − 1 . Now, compute ln ⁡ α 1 + ln ⁡ α = − e e − 1 1 − e e − 1 . Express the denominator with a common denominator: 1 − e e − 1 = e − 1 e − 1 − e e − 1 = − 1 e − 1 . Thus, − e e − 1 − 1 e − 1 = e 1 = e . The final result is ln ⁡ α 1 + ln ⁡ α = e .",
