    "explanationEn": "Since the ellipse has its major axis along the y -axis, the denominator under y 2 must be bigger than the denominator under x 2 . So we need f ( 3 a + 15 ) > f ( a 2 + 7 a + 3 ) . Given that f is a strictly decreasing positive function, a bigger function value happens when the input is smaller. So, 3 a + 15 a 2 + 7 a + 3. Bring all terms to one side: a 2 + 7 a + 3 − 3 a − 15 > 0 a 2 + 4 a − 12 > 0. Complete the square: a 2 + 4 a − 12 = ( a + 2 ) 2 − 16. So the inequality becomes ( a + 2 ) 2 − 16 > 0 ⇒ ( a + 2 ) 2 > 16. Taking square roots, | a + 2 | > 4 ⇒ a + 2 > 4 or a + 2 − 4. So, a > 2 or a − 6. That means the allowed values are a ∈ R − [ − 6 , 2 ] . Hence, α = − 6 and β = 2 . Therefore, α 2 + β 2 = ( − 6 ) 2 + ( 2 ) 2 = 36 + 4 = 40.",
