    "explanationEn": "For two projectiles launched with the same initial speed u to have the same horizontal range R, their angles of projection must be complementary. Let the first angle be θ . Then the second angle must be ( 90 ∘ − θ ) . The time taken for the projectile to return to the same horizontal level. T = 2 u sin ⁡ θ g ... ( i ) And the total horizontal distance covered is the range of projectile, R . R = u 2 sin ⁡ ( 2 θ ) g = 2 u 2 sin ⁡ θ cos ⁡ θ g ⇒ R = 2 u 2 sin ⁡ θ cos ⁡ θ g . . . . . . . . ( i i ) For the first body ( T 1 = 5 s ) : T 1 = 2 u sin ⁡ θ g ⇒ sin ⁡ θ = g T 1 2 u For the second body ( T 2 = 10 s ): T 2 = 2 u sin ⁡ ( 90 ∘ − θ ) g ⇒ cos ⁡ θ = g T 2 2 u ⇒ T 1 × T 2 = ( 2 u sin ⁡ θ g ) × ( 2 u cos ⁡ θ g ) ⇒ T 1 T 2 = 2 g ( 2 u 2 sin ⁡ θ cos ⁡ θ g ) Using the relation (ii) T 1 T 2 = 2 R g ⇒ R = g T 1 T 2 2 Here, the time of flight of first projectile is T 1 = 5 s and that of second projectile is T 2 = 10 s Putting the values in the formula of horizontal range, R = 10 × 5 × 10 2 ⇒ R = 250 m Therefore, the value of the horizontal range R is 250 m. Hence, the correct option is (A).",
