    "explanationEn": "The cylinder is slipping, which means its translational motion and rotational motion are not in order ( v = r ω ) for pure rolling. Initial translational velocity is v 0 = 49 m / s . Initial angular velocity is ω 0 = v 0 4 R , where R is the radius of solid cylinder of length L . For pure rolling to start, the condition v = ω R must be satisfied. Initially, ω 0 R = v 0 4 , which is less than v 0 , so the cylinder is sliding forward. Since the cylinder is sliding forward, kinetic friction ( f k ) acts backward at the point of contact. f k = μ k N = μ k mg . Using Newton's second law of motion ( F = ma ) linear retardation of cylinder is, F = ma ⇒ − μ k mg = ma ⇒ a = − μ k g Friction provides a torque ( τ ) about the center of mass. τ = f k ⋅ R = ( μ k mg ) R We also know τ = I α . For a solid cylinder, the moment of inertia I = 1 2 mR 2 . ( μ k mg ) R = ( 1 2 mR 2 ) α ⇒ α = 2 μ k g R We need to find the time t when the final translational velocity v and final angular velocity ω satisfy v = ω R . Using equation of linear motion, final linear velocity is v = v 0 + at = v 0 − μ k gt Using equation of rotational motion, final angular velocity is, ω = ω 0 + α t = v 0 4 R + 2 μ k g R t Applying the rolling condition v = ω R : v 0 − μ k gt = ( v 0 4 R + 2 μ k g R t ) R ⇒ v 0 − μ k gt = v 0 4 + 2 μ k gt ⇒ v 0 − v 0 4 = 2 μ k gt + μ k gt ⇒ 3 v 0 4 = 3 μ k gt ⇒ t = v 0 4 μ k g Substituting the given values, v 0 = 49 m / s , μ k = 0.25 and g = 9.8 m / s 2 t = 49 4 × 0.25 × 9.8 ⇒ t = 49 9.8 s = 5 s Therefore, the time taken for the cylinder to start rolling is 5 seconds. Hence, the correct option is (B).",
