    "shift": 2,
    "subject": "Physics",
    "questionEn": "One mole of diatomic gas having rotational modes only is kept in a cylinder with a piston system. The cross-section area of the cylinder is 4 cm 2 . The gas is heated slowly to raise the temperature by 1.2 ∘ C during which the piston moves by 25 mm . The amount of heat supplied to the gas is _ _ _ _ J. (Atmospheric pressure = 100 kPa , R = 8.3 J / mol . K ) (Neglect mass of the piston)",
