    "explanationEn": "According to Faraday's Law, a change in the magnetic flux ( Φ ) through a coil induces an electromotive force (e.m.f.) in that coil. The magnitude of the induced e.m.f. ( ε ) is given by: ε = N d Φ d t Where N is the total number of turns. For a solenoid, the magnetic flux Φ through each turn is Φ = B ⋅ A , where B is the magnetic field inside the solenoid and A is the cross-sectional area. The magnetic field B inside an ideal solenoid is: B = μ 0 nI Where μ 0 is the permeability of free space ( 4 π × 10 − 7 T ⋅ m A ) , n is the number of turns per unit length and I is the current. The total flux linkage is Ψ = N Φ = ( n l ) ( B A ) = ( n l ) ( μ 0 n I A ) = μ 0 n 2 l A I . Since ε = d Ψ dt , ε = L dI dt Where the self-inductance L is L = μ 0 n 2 lA The length of the solenoid is l = 30 cm = 0.3 m Turns per cm = 10 , so turns per meter will be n = 10 × 100 = 1000 turns / m . The area of cross-section is A = 5 cm 2 = 5 × 10 − 4 m 2 . So, L = ( 4 × 3.14 × 10 − 7 ) × ( 1000 ) 2 × 0.3 × ( 5 × 10 − 4 ) ⇒ L = 12.56 × 10 − 7 × 10 6 × 0.3 × 5 × 10 − 4 ⇒ L = 12.56 × 1.5 × 10 − 5 = 18.84 × 10 − 5 H The change in current is Δ I = 4 A − 2 A = 2 A . The time interval ( Δ t ) is 3.14 s. ε = L Δ I Δ t ⇒ ε = ( 18.84 × 10 − 5 ) × 2 3.14 ⇒ ε = 6 × 2 × 10 − 5 ⇒ ε = 12 × 10 − 5 V = α × 10 − 5 V ⇒ α = 12 Therefore, the value of α is 12 . Hence, the correct option is (B).",
