    "explanationEn": "Let us find the reflected points R and S , and then use vectors to get the area of parallelogram P Q R S . 1. Reflection of P ( 0 , − 5 , 0 ) in the line x − 1 2 = y 1 = z + 1 − 2 Write the line in parametric form: x = 1 + 2 t , y = t , z = − 1 − 2 t So, a point on the line is A ( 1 , 0 , − 1 ) and its direction vector is d ⃗ 1 = ( 2 , 1 , − 2 ) To reflect point P in the line, first find the foot of perpendicular from P to the line. Let the foot be M = A + t d ⃗ 1 = ( 1 + 2 t , t , − 1 − 2 t ) Since P M ⟂ d ⃗ 1 , ( P M ⃗ ) ⋅ d ⃗ 1 = 0 Now, P M ⃗ = M − P = ( 1 + 2 t , t + 5 , − 1 − 2 t ) So, ( 1 + 2 t , t + 5 , − 1 − 2 t ) ⋅ ( 2 , 1 , − 2 ) = 0 2 ( 1 + 2 t ) + ( t + 5 ) + ( − 2 ) ( − 1 − 2 t ) = 0 2 + 4 t + t + 5 + 2 + 4 t = 0 9 + 9 t = 0 t = − 1 Hence, M = ( 1 + 2 ( − 1 ) , − 1 , − 1 − 2 ( − 1 ) ) = ( − 1 , − 1 , 1 ) Since M is the midpoint of P R , R = 2 M − P R = 2 ( − 1 , − 1 , 1 ) − ( 0 , − 5 , 0 ) = ( − 2 , 3 , 2 ) So, R = ( − 2 , 3 , 2 ) 2. Reflection of Q ( 0 , − 1 2 , 0 ) in the line x − 1 − 1 = y + 9 4 = z + 1 1 Write the line in parametric form: x = 1 − u , y = − 9 + 4 u , z = − 1 + u So, a point on the line is B ( 1 , − 9 , − 1 ) and direction vector is d ⃗ 2 = ( − 1 , 4 , 1 ) Let the foot of perpendicular from Q to this line be N = B + u d ⃗ 2 = ( 1 − u , − 9 + 4 u , − 1 + u ) Since Q N ⟂ d ⃗ 2 , ( Q N ⃗ ) ⋅ d ⃗ 2 = 0 Now, Q N ⃗ = N − Q = ( 1 − u , − 9 + 4 u + 1 2 , − 1 + u ) = ( 1 − u , − 17 2 + 4 u , − 1 + u ) So, ( 1 − u , − 17 2 + 4 u , − 1 + u ) ⋅ ( − 1 , 4 , 1 ) = 0 − ( 1 − u ) + 4 ( − 17 2 + 4 u ) + ( − 1 + u ) = 0 − 1 + u − 34 + 16 u − 1 + u = 0 18 u − 36 = 0 u = 2 Hence, N = ( 1 − 2 , − 9 + 8 , − 1 + 2 ) = ( − 1 , − 1 , 1 ) Again, N is the midpoint of Q S , so S = 2 N − Q S = 2 ( − 1 , − 1 , 1 ) − ( 0 , − 1 2 , 0 ) = ( − 2 , − 2 + 1 2 , 2 ) = ( − 2 , − 3 2 , 2 ) So, S = ( − 2 , − 3 2 , 2 ) 3. Check the parallelogram sides Now, P = ( 0 , − 5 , 0 ) , Q = ( 0 , − 1 2 , 0 ) , R = ( − 2 , 3 , 2 ) , S = ( − 2 , − 3 2 , 2 ) Take adjacent sides from P : P Q ⃗ = Q − P = ( 0 , 9 2 , 0 ) and P R ⃗ = R − P = ( − 2 , 8 , 2 ) Also, Q S ⃗ = S − Q = ( − 2 , − 1 , 2 ) which is not equal to P R ⃗ , so let us check the correct order of parallelogram. Observe: P S ⃗ = S − P = ( − 2 , 7 2 , 2 ) and Q R ⃗ = R − Q = ( − 2 , 7 2 , 2 ) Thus, P S ∥ Q R . Also, P Q ⃗ = ( 0 , 9 2 , 0 ) , S R ⃗ = R − S = ( 0 , 9 2 , 0 ) So the correct parallelogram order is P Q R S , with adjacent sides P Q ⃗ and P S ⃗ Hence area of parallelogram is ∣ P Q ⃗ × P S ⃗ ∣ 4. Compute cross product P Q ⃗ = ( 0 , 9 2 , 0 ) , P S ⃗ = ( − 2 , 7 2 , 2 ) P Q ⃗ × P S ⃗ = ∣ i ˆ j ˆ k ˆ 0 9 2 0 − 2 7 2 2 ∣ = i ˆ ( 9 2 ⋅ 2 − 0 ⋅ 7 2 ) − j ˆ ( 0 ⋅ 2 − 0 ⋅ ( − 2 ) ) + k ˆ ( 0 ⋅ 7 2 − 9 2 ⋅ ( − 2 ) ) = 9 i ˆ + 0 j ˆ + 9 k ˆ So, ∣ P Q ⃗ × P S ⃗ ∣ = √ 9 2 + 9 2 = √ 162 = 9 √ 2 Therefore, the square of the area is ( 9 √ 2 ) 2 = 162 162",
