    "explanationEn": "Let the mean of the 20 observations be x ̄ and the standard deviation be σ . We are given: ∑ 20 i = 1 ( x i + 5 ) 2 = 2500 and ∑ 20 i = 1 ( x i − 5 ) 2 = 100 We will expand both expressions. First, ∑ 20 i = 1 ( x i + 5 ) 2 = ∑ 20 i = 1 ( x 2 i + 10 x i + 25 ) = ∑ x 2 i + 10 ∑ x i + 20 ⋅ 25 = ∑ x 2 i + 10 ∑ x i + 500 So, ∑ x 2 i + 10 ∑ x i + 500 = 2500 ∑ x 2 i + 10 ∑ x i = 2000 . . . ( 1 ) Now expand the second one: ∑ 20 i = 1 ( x i − 5 ) 2 = ∑ 20 i = 1 ( x 2 i − 10 x i + 25 ) = ∑ x 2 i − 10 ∑ x i + 500 So, ∑ x 2 i − 10 ∑ x i + 500 = 100 ∑ x 2 i − 10 ∑ x i = − 400 . . . ( 2 ) Now add (1) and (2): 2 ∑ x 2 i = 1600 ∑ x 2 i = 800 Now subtract (2) from (1): 20 ∑ x i = 2400 ∑ x i = 120 Hence mean: x ̄ = ∑ x i 20 = 120 20 = 6 Now use the formula for standard deviation: σ = √ ∑ x 2 i 20 − x ̄ 2 = √ 800 20 − 6 2 = √ 40 − 36 = √ 4 = 2 Therefore, the ratio of mean to standard deviation is x ̄ : σ = 6 : 2 = 3 : 1 So, the correct option is: 3 : 1 Option B",
