    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "For f ( θ ) = α tan 2 ⁡ θ + β cot 2 ⁡ θ and g ( θ ) = α sin 2 ⁡ θ + β cos 2 ⁡ θ , α > β > 0 we are given that min 0 θ π 2 f ( θ ) = max 0 θ π g ( θ ) . We will first find these two values. 1. Minimum value of f ( θ ) Let x = tan 2 ⁡ θ . Since 0 θ π 2 , we have x > 0 . Then cot 2 ⁡ θ = 1 tan 2 ⁡ θ = 1 x . So f ( θ ) = α x + β x . Now use the standard result for x > 0 : a x + b x ≥ 2 √ a b . Hence, α x + β x ≥ 2 √ α β . Therefore, min f ( θ ) = 2 √ α β . 2. Maximum value of g ( θ ) We have g ( θ ) = α sin 2 ⁡ θ + β cos 2 ⁡ θ . Using cos 2 ⁡ θ = 1 − sin 2 ⁡ θ , we get g ( θ ) = α sin 2 ⁡ θ + β ( 1 − sin 2 ⁡ θ ) = β + ( α − β ) sin 2 ⁡ θ . Since α > β , the coefficient of sin 2 ⁡ θ is positive. So g ( θ ) is maximum when sin 2 ⁡ θ = 1. For 0 θ π , this happens at θ = π 2 . Thus, max g ( θ ) = β + ( α − β ) = α . 3. Use the given condition Given min f ( θ ) = max g ( θ ) , so 2 √ α β = α . Now square both sides: 4 α β = α 2 . Since α > 0 , divide by α : 4 β = α . So, α = 4 β . 4. G.P. data First term: a = α 2 β = 4 β 2 β = 2. Common ratio: r = 2 β α = 2 β 4 β = 1 2 . So the G.P. is 2 , 1 , 1 2 , 1 4 , ... 5. Sum of first 10 terms For a G.P., S n = a ( 1 − r n ) 1 − r , r ≠ 1. Thus, S 10 = 2 ( 1 − ( 1 2 ) 10 ) 1 − 1 2 . Now simplify: S 10 = 2 ⋅ 1 − 1 1024 1 2 = 2 ⋅ 2 ( 1 − 1 1024 ) = 4 ⋅ 1023 1024 = 4092 1024 = 1023 256 . So, m n = 1023 256 . Hence, m + n = 1023 + 256 = 1279. Therefore, the answer is 1279 .",
