    "questionEn": "Two blocks ( P and Q ) with respectively masses 2 kg and 1.5 kg are joined by a massless thread. These blocks are mounted on a frictionless pully which is fixed on the edge of a cube ( S ) , as shown in the figure below. Block P is positioned on the top surface which has no friction and block Q is in contact with side-surface, having coefficient friction μ . The cube ( S ) moves towards the right with acceleration of g 2 , where g is gravitational acceleration. During this movement the block P and Q remain stationary. The value of μ is _ _ _ _ (take g = 10 m / s 2 )",
