    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "For the cell, the two reduction potentials are: M x + + x e − → M ( s ) , E ∘ red = + 0.15 V and Fe 3 + + 3 e − → Fe ( s ) , E ∘ red = − 0.036 V Since the reduction potential of M x + / M is greater, it will act as the cathode. So, Cathode: M x + + x e − → M ( s ) Anode: Fe ( s ) → Fe 3 + + 3 e − Hence, E ∘ cell = E ∘ cathode − E ∘ anode = 0.15 − ( − 0.036 ) = 0.186 V Now use the Nernst equation: E cell = E ∘ cell − 0.059 n log ⁡ Q Given: E cell = 0.2057 V , Q = 10 − 2 Since log ⁡ 10 − 2 = − 2 , 0.2057 = 0.186 − 0.059 n ( − 2 ) 0.2057 = 0.186 + 0.118 n 0.2057 − 0.186 = 0.118 n 0.0197 = 0.118 n n = 0.118 0.0197 ≈ 5.99 ≈ 6 So the number of electrons transferred in the balanced cell reaction is n = 6 Now, for balancing electrons: Oxidation of iron gives 3 electrons Reduction of M x + consumes x electrons Therefore, total electrons transferred in the balanced equation will be LCM ( 3 , x ) . Given this is 6 , we get: LCM ( 3 , x ) = 6 Possible values of x are 2 or 6 . Now it is given that M is a p-block metal. Common p-block metals generally form ions like 2 + , 3 + , 4 + , etc. Among the possible values, the most suitable is x = 2 So, the nearest integer value of x is 2",
