    "explanationEn": "For a diatomic gas (assuming no vibrational modes), the degrees of freedom f = 5 . The molar specific heat at constant volume for diatomic gas is C v = f 2 R = 5 2 R The molar specific heat at constant pressure is C p = C v + R = 5 2 R + R = 7 2 R The heat supplied at constant pressure is Δ Q = n C p Δ T = 7 2 n R Δ T The change in internal energy is Δ U = n C v Δ T = 5 2 n R Δ T The work done at constant pressure is Δ W = P Δ V From ideal gas equation, P V = n R T → P Δ V = n R Δ T So, the work done at constant pressure is Δ W = P Δ V = n R Δ T = 2 2 n R Δ T So, the ratio Δ Q : Δ U : Δ W is: 7 2 : 5 2 : 2 2 → 7 : 5 : 2 Therefore, the correct option is (D).",
