    "explanationEn": "In single slit diffraction, the condition for the n th minimum is: a sin ⁡ θ = n λ Where, λ is the wavelength of incident light on slit width of a . For the first minimum ( n = 1 ) , Assuming the angle θ is small such that sin ⁡ θ ≈ θ (in radians): θ = λ a The central maximum extends from the first minimum on one side to the first minimum on the other side. Therefore, the total angular width ( 2 θ ) in radians is: 2 θ = 2 λ a To convert the angular width from radians to degrees, we multiply by 180 π : Width in degrees = ( 2 λ a ) × 180 π The wavelength of light is λ = 628 nm = 628 × 10 − 9 m The slit width is a = 0.2 mm = 0.2 × 10 − 3 m So, β = 2 × 628 × 10 − 9 0.2 × 10 − 3 × 180 3.14 β = 1256 × 10 − 6 0.2 × 57.32 β = 6280 × 10 − 6 × 57.32 ≈ 0.36 degrees = α × 10 − 2 degrees = 0.36 degrees 36 × 10 − 2 = α × 10 − 2 α = 36 Therefore, the value of α is 36. Thus, the correct answer is 36.",
