    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "The given equation is: x d y d x − y = x 2 cot ⁡ x To get it into the standard form d y d x + P ( x ) y = Q ( x ) , we divide the entire equation by x : d y d x − 1 x y = x cot ⁡ x Here, P ( x ) = − 1 x and Q ( x ) = x cot ⁡ x . Finding the Integrating Factor (I.F.) The integrating factor is calculated as: I.F. = e ∫ P ( x ) d x = e ∫ − 1 x d x = e − ln ⁡ x = e ln ⁡ ( x − 1 ) = 1 x The solution to the differential equation is: y ⋅ ( I . F . ) = ∫ Q ( x ) ⋅ ( I . F . ) d x y x = ∫ ( x cot ⁡ x ) ⋅ 1 x d x y x = ∫ cot ⁡ x d x y x = ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ x ) + C y = x ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ x ) + C x Applying the Initial Condition We are given y ( π 2 ) = π 2 . Plugging these values in: π 2 = π 2 ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ π 2 ) + C ( π 2 ) So, the particular solution is y = x ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ x ) + x . We need to find the value of 6 y ( π 6 ) − 8 y ( π 4 ) . Calculate y ( π 6 ) : y ( π 6 ) = π 6 ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ π 6 ) + π 6 = π 6 ln ⁡ ( 1 2 ) + π 6 = π 6 ( 1 − ln ⁡ 2 ) Calculate y ( π 4 ) : y ( π 4 ) = π 4 ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ π 4 ) + π 4 = π 4 ln ⁡ ( 1 √ 2 ) + π 4 = π 4 ln ⁡ ( 2 − 1 / 2 ) + π 4 = π 4 ( 1 − 1 2 ln ⁡ 2 ) Calculate y ( π 4 ) : y ( π 4 ) = π 4 ln ⁡ ( sin ⁡ π 4 ) + π 4 = π 4 ln ⁡ ( 1 √ 2 ) + π 4 = π 4 ln ⁡ ( 2 − 1 / 2 ) + π 4 = π 4 ( 1 − 1 2 ln ⁡ 2 ) Now, substitute these into the expression: 6 y ( π 6 ) − 8 y ( π 4 ) = 6 [ π 6 ( 1 − ln ⁡ 2 ) ] − 8 [ π 4 ( 1 − 1 2 ln ⁡ 2 ) ] = π ( 1 − ln ⁡ 2 ) − 2 π ( 1 − 1 2 ln ⁡ 2 ) = π − π ln ⁡ 2 − 2 π + π ln ⁡ 2 = − π",
