    "explanationEn": "Given ∑ r = 1 25 ( r r 4 + r 2 + 1 ) = p q The expression r 4 + r 2 + 1 can be factored using a completion of squares technique: r 4 + r 2 + 1 = ( r 4 + 2 r 2 + 1 ) − r 2 = ( r 2 + 1 ) 2 − r 2 Using the difference of squares formula, a 2 − b 2 = ( a − b ) ( a + b ) : r 4 + r 2 + 1 = ( r 2 − r + 1 ) ( r 2 + r + 1 ) Split into Partial Fractions Now, let's rewrite the general term T r : T r = r ( r 2 − r + 1 ) ( r 2 + r + 1 ) We can express the numerator r in terms of the factors in the denominator: ( r 2 + r + 1 ) − ( r 2 − r + 1 ) = 2 r So, r = 1 2 [ ( r 2 + r + 1 ) − ( r 2 − r + 1 ) ] . Substituting this back: T r = 1 2 [ ( r 2 + r + 1 ) − ( r 2 − r + 1 ) ( r 2 − r + 1 ) ( r 2 + r + 1 ) ] T r = 1 2 [ 1 r 2 − r + 1 − 1 r 2 + r + 1 ] Evaluate the Telescoping Sum Let f ( r ) = 1 r 2 − r + 1 . Note that f ( r + 1 ) = 1 ( r + 1 ) 2 − ( r + 1 ) + 1 = 1 r 2 + 2 r + 1 − r − 1 + 1 = 1 r 2 + r + 1 . Our sum becomes : S = 1 2 ∑ r = 1 25 [ f ( r ) − f ( r + 1 ) ] Expanding this: For r = 1 : f ( 1 ) − f ( 2 ) For r = 2 : f ( 2 ) − f ( 3 ) For r = 3 : f ( 3 ) − f ( 4 ) … For r = 24 : f ( 24 ) − f ( 25 ) For r = 25 : f ( 25 ) − f ( 26 ) Result of summation: ∑ r = 1 25 [ f ( r ) − f ( r + 1 ) ] = f ( 1 ) − f ( 26 ) So, S = 1 2 [ f ( 1 ) − f ( 26 ) ] Calculate the Final Value f ( 1 ) = 1 1 2 − 1 + 1 = 1 f ( 26 ) = 1 25 2 + 25 + 1 = 1 625 + 25 + 1 = 1 651 S = 1 2 [ 1 − 1 651 ] = 1 2 ( 651 − 1 651 ) = 650 2 × 651 S = 325 651 325 = ( 5 ) 2 × 13 and 651 = 3 × 7 × 31 they share no common factor gcd ⁡ ( 325 , 651 ) = 1 So p = 325 and q = 651 ∴ p + q = 325 + 651 = 976",
