    "explanationEn": "1) Find X for [ Pt ( NH 3 ) ( H 2 O ) BrCl ] Pt in such complexes is usually Pt ( II ) , which (as per NCERT) forms square planar complexes. The complex is of type [ MABCD ] (four different ligands). For square planar [ MABCD ] , the number of geometrical isomers is 3 (based on which ligand is trans to a chosen ligand; distinct trans-pairings give 3 arrangements). So, X = 3. 2) Find Y for [ CrCl 2 ( ox ) 2 ] 3 − Here ox (oxalate) is a bidentate ligand. Two oxalate ligands occupy 4 coordination positions, and 2 positions are occupied by Cl − . So the complex is octahedral of type [ M ( AA ) 2 B 2 ] . Such complexes show cis–trans isomerism: cis form is optically active (exists as Δ and Λ enantiomers) trans form is optically inactive So optically inactive isomers = only 1 (trans) . Thus, Y = 1. 3) Find Z for [ Co ( NH 3 ) 3 ( NO 2 ) 3 ] This is an octahedral complex of type [ MA 3 B 3 ] . It shows fac–mer isomerism: fac mer So, Z = 2. Final Answer X + Y + Z = 3 + 1 + 2 = 6. 6",
