    "questionEn": "Let y = x be the equation of a chord of the circle C 1 (in the closed half-plane x ≥ 0 ) of diameter 10 passing through the origin. Let C 2 be another circle described on the given chord as its diameter. If the equation of the chord of the circle C 2 , which passes through the point ( 2 , 3 ) and is farthest from the center of C 2 , is x + a y + b = 0 , then a − b is equal to",
