    "explanationEn": "The moment of inertia of a uniform solid cylinder of mass M and radius R about its central axis is given by : I = 1 2 MR 2 If area of cross-section of the cylinder is A and length is L then volume is, V = π R 2 L If the density of the cylinder is ρ and volume is V , then the mass of the cylinder is, m = ρ V Putting in the expression for the moment of inertia, I = 1 2 [ ρ π R 2 L ] × R 2 = π ρ R 4 L 2 For the larger cylinder, ρ 1 = ρ , the radius is R 1 = R and the length is L 1 = L So, the moment of inertia of the larger cylinder is, I 1 = π ρ 1 R 4 1 L 1 2 = π ρ R 4 L 2 For the smaller cylinder, as it is carved from the same material, so it has the same density ( ρ 2 = ρ ). The radius is R 2 = R / 3 and the length is L 2 = L / 2 So, the moment of inertia of the smaller cylinder is, I 2 = π ρ 2 R 4 2 L 2 2 = π ρ ( R 3 ) 4 ( L 2 ) 2 = π ρ R 4 L 324 Now, the ratio of the moment of inertia of larger cylinder to the smaller cylinder is, I 1 I 2 = ( π ρ R 4 L 2 ) ( π ρ R 4 L 324 ) = 324 2 = 162 Therefore, the value of ratio of moment of inertia is I 1 I 2 = 162 . Hence, the correct answer is 162 .",
