    "explanationEn": "For a constant volume process, the heat supplied ( Q ) is given by the formula : Q = n C v Δ T Where : 1. n = number of moles of the gas. 2. C v = molar specific heat capacity at constant volume. 3. Δ T = change in temperature 50 ∘ C − 20 ∘ C = 30 ∘ C = 30 K We are given the molar specific heat at constant pressure, C p = 7 2 R . Using Mayer's Relation ( C p − C v = R ) : C v = C p − R ⇒ C v = 7 2 R − R = 5 2 R Using the formula of heat, 300 = n × ( 5 2 × 8.314 ) × 30 n = 300 × 2 5 × 8.314 × 30 ≈ 0.481 moles So, the amount of the gas is 0.481 moles. As the molar mass of the gas is not given in the question, we can't determine the mass of the gas directly.",
