    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "Carbanion means a carbon atom carrying a negative charge. Such a species is stable when this negative charge is reduced (spread out) or pulled away. If a group attached to the carbanion is electron withdrawing (shows − I effect), it pulls electron density towards itself. This reduces the negative charge on carbon, so the carbanion becomes more stable . If a group attached to the carbanion is electron donating (shows + I effect), it pushes electron density towards the carbon. This increases the negative charge on carbon, so the carbanion becomes less stable . So, while arranging in decreasing order of stability: carbanions with stronger electron withdrawing groups will be more stable, and those with electron donating groups will be less stable.",
