    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "The electric potential V due to a charged spherical shell of radius R and charge Q is given by : V = ⎧⎩⎨ ⎪ ⎪ 1 4 π ε 0 Q R , r R 1 4 π ε 0 Q R , r = R 1 4 π ε 0 Q r , r > R Point A is on the surface of shell A, inside shell B, and inside shell C. The total potential is the sum of potentials due to each shell (Superposition Principle). So, the potential at A ; 1. Due to A (Surface, r = a ) ⇒ V AA = k q 1 a 2. Due to B (Inside, r b ) ⇒ V AB = kq 2 b 3. Due to C (Inside, r c ) ⇒ V AC = kq 3 c Hence, total potential at point A is, V A = ( kq 1 a + kq 2 b + kq 3 c ) = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 a + q 2 b + q 3 c ) For the point B which is outside shell A , on the surface of shell B , and inside shell C . So, the potential at point B, 1. Due to A (Outside, distance b ) ⇒ V BA = k q 1 b 2. Due to B (Surface, r = b ) ⇒ V BB = kq 2 b 3. Due to C (Inside, r c ) ⇒ V BC = kq 3 c Hence, total potential at point B is: V B = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 b + q 2 b + q 3 c ) ⇒ V B = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 + q 2 b + q 3 c ) Point C is outside shell A , outside shell B , and on the surface of shell C . So, potential at point C is, 1. Due to A (Outside, distance c ) ⇒ V CA = kq 1 c 2. Due to B (Outside, distance c ) ⇒ V CB = kq 2 c 3. Due to C (Surface, r = c ) ⇒ V CC = kq 3 c Hence, total potential at point C is : V C = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 c + q 2 c + q 3 c ) ⇒ V C = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 + q 2 + q 3 c ) So, V A = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 a + q 2 b + q 3 c ) , V B = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 + q 2 b + q 3 c ) , V C = 1 4 π ε 0 ( q 1 + q 2 + q 3 c ) . Hence, the correct option is (D).",
