    "explanationEn": "The work done ( W ) by an external agent to rearrange a system of masses against gravitational force is equal to the change in the Gravitational Potential Energy ( U ) of the system. W = Δ U = U final − U initial For a system of three masses m 1 , m 2 , m 3 separated by distances r 12 , r 23 , r 31 , the total potential energy is the sum of the potential energies of all pairs : U = U 12 + U 23 + U 31 = − G [ m 1 m 2 r 12 + m 2 m 3 r 23 + m 3 m 1 r 31 ] Since the masses are at the vertices of an equilateral triangle, all distances are equal ( r 12 = r 23 = r 31 = L ). U = − G L ( m 1 m 2 + m 2 m 3 + m 3 m 1 ) Given masses are, 1. m 1 = 200 kg 2. m 2 = 300 kg 3. m 3 = 400 kg U = − G L ( 200 × 300 + 300 × 400 + 400 × 200 ) = − G ( 2.6 × 10 5 ) L So, the work done by external agent is, W = U f − U i ⇒ W = [ − G ( 2.6 × 10 5 ) L f ] − [ − G ( 2.6 × 10 5 ) L i ] W = G ( 2.6 × 10 5 ) ( 1 L i − 1 L f ) The initial side is = L i = 20 m The final side is L f = 25 m Putting the values, W = ( 6.7 × 10 − 11 ) × ( 2.6 × 10 5 ) × ( 1 20 − 1 25 ) ⇒ W = ( 6.7 × 10 − 11 ) × ( 2.6 × 10 5 ) × ( 10 − 2 ) ⇒ W = 1.742 × 10 − 7 J Therefore, the work done in this process is 1.74 × 10 − 7 J . Hence, the correct option is (B).",
