    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "The problem states the gas is filled in a closed cylinder. That means the volume of the gas remains constant during the heating process ( V = constant). For a fixed mass of gas at constant volume, the pressure is directly proportional to the absolute temperature. P 1 T 1 = P 2 T 2 Initial pressure is P 1 = 3.23 kPa = 3.23 × 1000 Pa = 3230 Pa Initial temperature is T 1 = 50 ∘ C = ( 50 + 273 ) K = 323 K The final temperature is T 2 = 2 × T 1 = 2 × 323 K = 646 K Using the relation P 1 T 1 = P 2 T 2 : P 2 = P 1 × T 2 T 1 ⇒ P 2 = 3230 × 646 323 P 2 = 3230 × 2 = 6460 Pa Therefore, the modified pressure is 6460 Pa . Hence, the correct answer is 6460 . Other Solution : V = constant so P ∝ T T i = 50 ∘ C = 323 K T f = 100 ∘ C = 373 K ⇒ P f P i = T f T i ⇒ P f 3.23 kPa = 373 323 ⇒ P f = 3730 Pa",
