    "questionEn": "When an unpolarized light falls at a particular angle on a glass plate (placed in air), it is observed that the reflected beam is linearly polarized. The angle of refracted beam with respect to the normal is _ _ _ _ . ( tan − 1 ⁡ ( 1.52 ) = 57.7 ∘ , refractive indices of air and glass are 1.00 and 1.52, respectively.)",
