    "explanationEn": "In a series LCR circuit, the current reaches its maximum value when the circuit is at resonance. At resonance the inductive reactance ( X L ) equals the capacitive reactance ( X C ) . The total impedance ( Z ) is Z = √ R 2 + ( X L − X C ) 2 = R , purely resistive and minimum. So, the peak current is given by I 0 = V 0 Z = V 0 R . From the given equation of a.c. voltage is V = 5 sin ⁡ ( 100 t ) . So, the peak voltage is V 0 = 5 V The resistance is R = 100 Ω = Z . So, the calculated value of peak current is I 0 = 5 100 = 0.05 A = 50 mA . This shows that the circuit is in resonance state. From the voltage equation V = 5 sin ⁡ ( 100 t ) , ω = 100 rad / s Using the resonance condition X L = X C : ω L = 1 ω C ⇒ C = 1 ω 2 L Putting the values, we get C = 1 ( 100 ) 2 × 2 = 1 20000 F = 10 6 20000 μ F = 50 μ F Therefore, the capacitance of the capacitor is 50 μ F . Hence, the correct answer is 50.",
