    "questionEn": "A + 2 B ⟶ AB 2 36.0 g of 'A' (Molar mass : 60 g mol − 1 ) and 56.0 g of ' B ' (Molar mass : 80 g mol − 1 ) are allowed to react. Which of the following statements are correct ? A. 'A' is the limiting reagent. B. 77.0 g of AB 2 is formed. C. Molar mass of AB 2 is 140 g mol − 1 . D. 15.0 g of A is left unreacted after the completion of reaction. Choose the correct answer from the options given below :",
