    "questionEn": "A star has 100 % helium composition. It starts to convert three 4 He into one 12 C via triple alpha process as 4 He + 4 He + 4 He → 12 C + Q . The mass of the star is 2.0 × 10 32 kg and it generates energy at the rate of 5.808 × 10 30 W . The rate of converting these 4 He to 12 C is n × 10 42 s − 1 , where n is _________. [ Take, mass of 4 He = 4.0026 u , mass of 12 C = 12 u ]",
