    "explanationEn": "To solve for the angle of projection θ , we will first establish the relationship between the variables given and then derive the formula using kinematics. The time T for one revolution at speed v in a circle of radius R is related to the circumference of the circle by the formula: v = 2 π R T When the particle is projected with the same speed v at an angle θ to the horizontal, its vertical component of velocity is given by v y = v sin ⁡ θ . The maximum height H reached by the projectile can be found from the kinematic equation: H = v 2 y 2 g = ( v sin ⁡ θ ) 2 2 g We are given that the maximum height attained H is equal to 4 R , so: 4 R = ( v sin ⁡ θ ) 2 2 g Substitute v from the first equation into the second one: 4 R = ( ( 2 π R T ) sin ⁡ θ ) 2 2 g 4 R = ( 2 π R sin ⁡ θ ) 2 2 g T 2 4 R = 4 π 2 R 2 sin 2 ⁡ θ 2 g T 2 2 g T 2 = π 2 R sin 2 ⁡ θ Now solve for sin ⁡ θ : sin ⁡ θ = [ 2 g T 2 π 2 R ] 1 / 2 Finally, to solve for θ , take the inverse sine of both sides: θ = sin − 1 ⁡ ( [ 2 g T 2 π 2 R ] 1 / 2 ) Therefore, the correct answer is: Option A sin − 1 ⁡ [ 2 g T 2 π 2 R ] 1 / 2",
