    "questionEn": "The number of electrons present in all the completely filled subshells having n = 4 and s = + 1 2 is _______. (Where n = principal quantum number and s = spin quantum number)",
    "optionsEn": [
      "Value 1",
      "Value 2",
      "Value 3",
      "Value 4"
    ],
    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "To determine the number of electrons with a spin quantum number of s = + 1 2 in all completely filled subshells with principal quantum number n = 4 , we must first identify the subshells in the n=4 shell and then calculate the electrons with the specified spin. The n=4 shell has the following subshells and their capacity for electrons: 4 s subshell can hold 2 electrons 4 p subshell can hold 6 electrons 4 d subshell can hold 10 electrons 4 f subshell can hold 14 electrons In quantum mechanics, each orbital within these subshells can hold 2 electrons, each with opposite spins ( + 1 2 and − 1 2 ). Thus, in a completely filled subshell, half of the electrons will have a spin quantum number of + 1 2 : In 4 s , 1 out of 2 electrons will have s = + 1 2 In 4 p , 3 out of 6 electrons will have s = + 1 2 In 4 d , 5 out of 10 electrons will have s = + 1 2 In 4 f , 7 out of 14 electrons will have s = + 1 2 Adding these together: 1 + 3 + 5 + 7 = 16 electrons with s = + 1 2 in all completely filled subshells with n = 4 .",
