    "questionEn": "Two plates A and B have thermal conductivities 84 Wm − 1 K − 1 and 126 Wm − 1 K − 1 respectively. They have same surface area and same thickness. They are placed in contact along their surfaces. If the temperatures of the outer surfaces of A and B are kept at 100 ∘ C and 0 ∘ C respectively, then the temperature of the surface of contact in steady state is _____________ ∘ C .",
