    "questionEn": "KClO 3 + 6 FeSO 4 + 3 H 2 SO 4 → KCl + 3 Fe 2 ( SO 4 ) 3 + 3 H 2 O The above reaction was studied at 300 K by monitoring the concentration of FeSO 4 in which initial concentration was 10 M and after half an hour became 8.8 M. The rate of production of Fe 2 ( SO 4 ) 3 is _________ × 10 − 6 mol L − 1 s − 1 (Nearest integer)",
