    "explanationEn": "Let's consider the power P dissipated by a single heater filament with resistance R when connected to a voltage V . The power dissipated by the heater filament is given by: P = V 2 R When the two identical heater filaments are connected in parallel, the equivalent resistance R P is given by: 1 R P = 1 R + 1 R = 2 R ⇒ R P = R 2 The total power dissipated P P by the two filaments connected in parallel is: P P = V 2 R P = V 2 R 2 = 2 V 2 ⋅ 1 R = 2 P When the two identical heater filaments are connected in series, the equivalent resistance R S is given by: R S = R + R = 2 R The total power dissipated P S by the two filaments connected in series is: P S = V 2 R S = V 2 2 R = 1 2 V 2 ⋅ 1 R = 1 2 P Now, let's find the ratio of the heat produced in the same time for parallel to series connection: P P P S = 2 P 1 2 P = 2 P × 2 P = 4 P P = 4 : 1",
