    "questionEn": "A monochromatic light is incident on a hydrogen sample in ground state. Hydrogen atoms absorb a fraction of light and subsequently emit radiation of six different wavelengths. The frequency of incident light is x × 10 15 Hz . The value of x is ____________. (Given h = 4.25 × 10 − 15 eVs )",
