    "subject": "Physics",
    "questionEn": "An electron (mass m ) with an initial velocity v ⃗ = v 0 i ˆ ( v 0 > 0 ) is moving in an electric field E ⃗ = − E 0 i ˆ ( E 0 > 0 ) where E 0 is constant. If at t = 0 de Broglie wavelength is λ 0 = h m v 0 , then its de Broglie wavelength after time t is given by",
